# Purpose : README file for BusTalk simulations
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note: 
-----
At the start of each simulation session,
initialise the following environment variables:
For example..

# Set the peripheral path environment variable
setenv PERIPH /home/nbray/sfwork/snowdon/kmi_pl050

# Set up peripheral specific data variables
setenv PERIPHERAL Kmi
setenv PRODUCT PL050

set prompt = `hostname`':'`whoami`':PERIPH> '
# Set the technology library path environment variable

# For VHDL gate level simulations use Avant! CB25 VITAL
setenv LIB_VITAL $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/vhdl
# For Verilog gate level simulations use Avant! CB25 Verilog
setenv LIB_VERILOG $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/verilog
setenv LIB_UDP $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/verilog
setenv CELL_LIB CB25

The recommended method is to create a file, SourceMe, in kmi_pl050 directory,
containing the above commands, and run UNIX source SourceMe.
The directory paths above need amending for each specific installation.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running BusTalk simulations. 

Clock Enabled Tests - (Production)
----------------------------------
1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory 'make Kmi_prod'
  This will create invec/Kmi_prod.bif
  
  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/Kmi_prod.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Kmi_prod.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL RTL
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uut/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uut directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
    In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Kmi.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim tb_Kmi

- Use of the startup file (init.do) allows ModelSim to generate
  a toggle coverage report.

2. VHDL NETLIST simulations
---------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory 'make Kmi_prod'
  This will create invec/Kmi_prod.bif
  
  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/Kmi_prod.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Kmi_prod.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL NETLIST
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uutNetlist/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uutNetlist directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
    In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Kmi.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim -sdfmax u_Kmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21 \
    -L libvhdl tb_Kmi
  vsim -sdfmin u_Kmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21 \
    -L libvhdl tb_Kmi

Free Running Tests
------------------
1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory 'make Kmi_free'
  This will create invec/Kmi_free.bif
  
  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/Kmi_free.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Kmi_free.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/bustests directory 'make Kmi_free'
  This will create invec/Kmi_free.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL RTL
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uut/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uut directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
    In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Kmi_free.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim tb_Kmi_free

2. VHDL NETLIST simulations
---------------------------
- In the BusTalk/bustests directory 'make Kmi_free'
  This will create invec/Kmi_free.bif
  
  Change the link from BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.bif
  to the test vector file in BusTalk/bustests/invec/Kmi_free.bif
  For example,
  cd BusTalk/vhdl/tbench/
  ln -s ../../bustests/invec/Kmi_free.bif infile.bif

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL NETLIST
  uut = $PERIPH/vhdl/uutNetlist/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uutNetlist directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following file:
    In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_Kmi_free.vhd)

- In the BusTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim -sdfmax u_Kmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21 \
    -L libvhdl tb_Kmi_free
  vsim -sdfmin u_Kmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21 \
    -L libvhdl tb_Kmi_free

